{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["The reason for <b>then Moses and Aaron fell on their faces</b> — they saw that the people were plotting to appoint a leader and turn back immediately, so the righteous men rose and prostrated themselves on their faces to the ground to say to them: 'Please, my brothers, do not do wrong,' and let this not be a stumbling-block for you. Therefore Scripture says, <b>before all the congregation of the assembly of the children of Israel</b>, for it was before them that they prostrated themselves on their faces. Similarly, 'he fell on his face to the ground and bowed three times' (I Samuel 20:41). And the meaning of <b>before</b> is 'before them,' as in 'his brothers also went and fell down before him' (Genesis 50:18), and many others besides."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:05:05.663048510Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}